TASK-259 runtime harness: a required history permission switched off through
the Settings pane. Temporary code, never committed to Detour/. Gated on
DETOUR_VERIFY_DIR and DETOUR_VERIFY_EXT (an unpacked extension: permissions
history + storage, optional notifications, a worker answering
{type:'search'} with chrome.history.search). Data dir DetourVerify2590.
Installs the extension through ExtensionManager.install (unpacked), opens an
extension page, queries history.search from the page and through the worker,
opens Settings > Extensions, clicks the history switch (answering the
"Revoke Permission?" alert from a .modalPanel run-loop timer), queries again,
answers a permissions.request prompt (permissionPromptAnswerOverride) and
calls permissions.remove while logging the pane's notifications switch,
clicks history back on, then off, disables + enables the extension (context
reload) and queries a fresh page. Runner: launch with the two env vars,
serve SHOOT lines with screencapture -l, kill only the launched PID.

Results (2026-11-03): installed rows history/storage granted; page and
worker ok; pane history ON. After the click: row denied, pane OFF, page
"history permission not declared", worker "History permission not
declared". Prompt answer: row granted, pane notifications ON without a
reselect; remove: row gone, pane OFF. Switched on: row granted, ok from
both. Off + reload: row denied, pane OFF, refused from both.

